  "/api/bundles/{cookbook_id}/skills/bulk": {
   "post": {
    "description": "Add MANY skills (local and/or federated, mixed) to a bundle in ONE call.\n\nBulk = the demo (plan §P3.6 gate 4): \"select N skills → new bundle\" must\nbe one operation, not N HTTP calls. Authorization reuses the exact same\nownership predicate every other bundle-mutation route uses\n(``_resolve_owned_cookbook`` → ``authz.owner_match_within_tenant``) — a\nnon-owner gets the same 404-no-existence-leak every other route returns,\nresolved ONCE for the whole batch.\n\nPartial-failure: each item is attempted independently; the response\nalways has one ``BulkItemResult`` per input item, `ok` per item, and the\nwhole request only 4xxs on a REQUEST-level problem (bad auth, oversized\nbatch, cookbook not found) — never because one item was unresolvable.\n\nIdempotency: re-posting the same batch (including a batch that partially\nlanded) updates already-present members' `source` and reports\n``reactivated=True`` for them; it never duplicates a row (both a DB-level\nUniqueConstraint AND an in-request existing-row check enforce this).",
    "operationId": "add_skills_bulk_api_bundles__cookbook_id__skills_bulk_post",
    "parameters": [
     {
      "in": "path",
      "name": "cookbook_id",
      "required": true,
      "schema": {
       "title": "Cookbook Id",
       "type": "string"
      }
     }
    ],
    "requestBody": {
     "content": {
      "application/json": {
       "schema": {
        "$ref": "#/components/schemas/BulkAddIn"
       }
      }
